# The FineType release this repository stages into its artefacts.
#
# ONE line, reviewed, and every consumer reads it through
# scripts/finetype-pin.sh — scripts/fetch-finetype-bundle.sh (which turns it
# into bytes), scripts/package.sh (which checks the bytes it staged carry this
# version) and .github/workflows/release.yml (which names it in the run
# summary). scripts/check-finetype-pin.sh runs each of those readers and
# refuses when any of them answers with something else.
#
# WHY A PIN AND NOT A RANGE. Two builds of the same brightfield tag must stage
# the same bytes, and a bump must be a line somebody read. The cost, accepted
# deliberately: this pin can rot silently — brightfield could ship a classifier
# a year behind FineType and nothing here would say so. There is no scheduled
# bump; moving it is a pull request like any other.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES NOT SAY. Which model FineType built into that release. The
# model rides in the release's own model asset, so the tag decides it; the
# fetch script prints the name it found rather than asserting one, because
# asserting a model name here would be a second pin nobody reviewed against
# anything.
FINETYPE_TAG=v0.6.58
